#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:733
msgid "Vercel AI Gateway"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:735
msgid ""
"[Vercel AI Gateway](https://vercel.com/ai-gateway) provides access to many "
"models through a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:737
msgid ""
"Create an API key from your [Vercel AI Gateway keys page](https://vercel.com/"
"d?to=%2F%5Bteam%5D%2F%7E%2Fai%2Fapi-keys&title=Go+to+AI+Gateway)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:738
msgid ""
"Open the settings view (`agent: open settings`) and go to the **Vercel AI "
"Gateway** section"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:739
msgid "Enter your Vercel AI Gateway API key"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:741
msgid "The Vercel AI Gateway API key will be saved in your keychain."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:743
msgid ""
"Zed will also use the `VERCEL_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` environment variable if "
"it's defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:745
msgid ""
"You can also set a custom endpoint for Vercel AI Gateway in your settings "
"file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:750
msgid "\"vercel_ai_gateway\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:751
msgid "\"https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:757
msgid "Vercel v0"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:759
msgid ""
"[Vercel v0](https://v0.app/docs/api/model) is a model for generating full-"
"stack apps, with framework-aware completions for stacks like Next.js and "
"Vercel. It supports text and image inputs and provides fast streaming "
"responses."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:762
msgid ""
"The v0 models are [OpenAI-compatible models](/#openai-api-compatible), and "
"Vercel appears as a dedicated provider in the panel's settings view."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:764
msgid ""
"To start using it with Zed, ensure you have first created a [v0 API key]"
"(https://v0.dev/chat/settings/keys). Once you have it, paste it directly "
"into the Vercel provider section in the panel's settings view."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:767
msgid ""
"You should then find it as `v0-1.5-md` in the model dropdown in the Agent "
"Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:769
msgid "xAI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:771
msgid ""
"Zed includes a dedicated [xAI](https://x.ai/) provider. You can use your own "
"API key to access Grok models."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:773
msgid ""
"[Create an API key in the xAI Console](https://console.x.ai/team/default/api-"
"keys)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:774
msgid ""
"Open the settings view (`agent: open settings`) and go to the **xAI** section"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:775
msgid "Enter your xAI API key"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:777
msgid ""
"The xAI API key will be saved in your keychain. Zed will also use the "
"`XAI_API_KEY` environment variable if it's defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:779
msgid ""
"**Note:** The xAI API is OpenAI-compatible, and Zed also includes a "
"dedicated xAI provider. We recommend using the dedicated `x_ai` provider "
"configuration instead of the [OpenAI API Compatible](#openai-api-compatible) "
"method."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:783
msgid ""
"The Zed agent comes pre-configured with common Grok models. If you wish to "
"use alternate models or customize their parameters, you can do so by adding "
"the following to your Zed settings file ([how to edit](../configuring-zed."
"md#settings-files)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:788
msgid "\"x_ai\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/llm-providers.md:789
msgid "\"https://api.x.ai/v1\""
msgstr ""

